{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtN9CAfDx9qr2SqbTp48","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane, inside `sandbox/agent.sb`, the way the kimi lane does. I did not run a live Codex job, because that would send the task to OpenAI. I tested the plumbing with a stub `codex` on PATH, and the lane passed. The changes are uncommitted, and the details are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **`run.sh`**: new `codex-sandboxed` lane with an empty scratch `HOME`. Codex writes its `-o` file to a scratch folder in `/tmp`, which the lane copies into the run folder afterwards. If that file is missing, the lane exits 3 instead of 0.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: the hard-coded `~/.kimi-code` rule is now an `AGENT_HOME` parameter. Each lane opens only its own folder, so the kimi shell cannot read Codex's login. The kimi lane passes its own `AGENT_HOME`.\n- **`README.md`**: documents the lane. I also corrected a wrong claim that Codex logs in with `CODEX_API_KEY`. On this Mac it logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`, which is why the lane opens `~/.codex`.\n- **`codex` lane**: unchanged.\n\nOf the colleague's note, these parts applied: the `-o` write being denied inside the sandbox, exit 0 not proving the file was written, the stdout/stderr redirect handling, and the ground rules. Mistral Vibe does not apply, since this repo has no such lane. The `CODEX_API_KEY` login does not apply here.\n\nChecks I ran, with no model calls:\n- The script passes `bash -n`.\n- A sandbox probe with the lane's parameters: the agent can read and write `~/.codex`, and it cannot list or write the rest of the real home.\n- The kimi profile still parses and keeps `~/.codex` out of reach.\n- An end-to-end `fizz` run with the stub: the last message was copied into the run folder, and a run without the file exited 3. I then removed the test folders and the stub.\n\nNot verified:\n- Real Codex may write under the real home outside `~/.codex`, such as a cache. Those writes would be denied. Check the first live run's `agent.err` for `Operation not permitted`.\n- The kimi lane itself was not run, because `kimi` is not installed here.\n\nThe limit to know: the agent's shell can read `~/.codex/auth.json`, and the kimi lane has the same exposure with `~/.kimi-code`. A separate, limited API key would shrink that risk, but would not remove it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":57087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76c081c6-330e-4ab2-856b-873c5c653708","uuid":"a1019425-79c0-4f6b-abb1-f7db75fa57db","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:17:30.039Z","request_id":"req_011CgtN9Bz1Toac15r3dfTLA"}
